WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.362
The federal requirement, from
the guide's requirements table.

2
00:00:03.362 --> 00:00:07.153
Gate seven supports S I four,
system monitoring; A U six,

3
00:00:07.153 --> 00:00:13.097
enhancements one and three, automated
process integration and correlating audit

4
00:00:13.097 --> 00:00:15.509
record repositories; and C M three,

5
00:00:15.509 --> 00:00:19.300
configuration change control,
here for rule changes.

6
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:24.587
The evidence is the rule repository, the
test outputs and the deployed-rules export.

7
00:00:24.587 --> 00:00:30.764
Gate eight supports S I four; A U six,
enhancement three, correlating repositories;

8
00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:36.112
and A C two, enhancement twelve,
account monitoring for atypical usage.

9
00:00:36.112 --> 00:00:40.212
The evidence is the correlation
query output and the sensors' health.

10
00:00:40.212 --> 00:00:44.925
All from NIST special publication eight
hundred fifty-three, revision five.

11
00:00:44.925 --> 00:00:49.031
Each row lines up with fed-ramp
twenty X key security indicators,

12
00:00:49.031 --> 00:00:54.300
which bind cloud service providers; the
agency lines its own evidence up with them.

13
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.390
The gates support these controls,

14
00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:59.660
and the assessor decides
whether each is satisfied.
